WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.790 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hello and welcome to playstation grenade  september is back again the month where  the games industry starts cranking back  into motion this is the series in which  we outline the best games each month has  to offer from the full price behemoths  to the reduced and totally free-to-play  games so here's eight i think are worth  your time cue the music  arguably the biggest game of the month  is death loop an xbox owned game which  is only available on playstation and pc  it's a strange world we live in death  loop is described as a murder puzzle in  which we play an assassin trapped in a  time loop  set in first person we repeat the same  day over and over and over again the  twist is to end the loop you must take  out eight targets in a single day should  we die it all starts again you're in a  death loop my friend along the way  you'll upgrade your character's  abilities including a way to lift twice  in a single loop bending reality to suit  your playstyle whether that's all out  attack or teleporting to unseen  locations and dealing damage from the  shadows oh and there's also another  assassin here just to kill you and  they're better than you so you're gonna  die a lot death loop hits ps5 and pc on  september 14th and once the timed  exclusivity deal runs out xbox will have  this too  [Music]  next kinah bridge of spirits are you  getting deja vu that's because kina was  scheduled to release last month but  moments after i made this video last  month it was delayed until september  21st kina is a spirit guide helping  people trapped between the living world  and the dead find their way to the  afterlife essentially kina is heavily  inspired by legend of zelda which shines  through constantly i'd previously  described it as breath of the wild meets  pikmin mainly because of these cute rock  creatures who are here to help keena  along the way there'll be puzzles to  figure out there'll be exploration to  lose yourself in and a fighting system  which evolves throughout the game and it  just looks gorgeous too hopefully it  does release this time and if it does it  will be on september 21st on ps4 ps5 and  pc here's an interesting one fist forged  in shadow torch okay not the greatest  name ever but this could be a hidden gem  at a hugely reduced price over here in  the uk it's just 25 quid fist has us  playing a rabbit with a mechanical arm  attached to his back  essentially fist is a side scroller with  platforming elements and a bunch of hack  and slash fighting mechanics to get used  to with combos to master too and i even  saw some bullet hell sections we don't  know much about fist but we do know it  hits ps5 and ps4 on september 7th which  so happens to be ps plus day hmm i  wonder if this could be one of the three  games it's unlikely as the pre-orders  are available now but i wouldn't be  surprised if i'm honest and if it isn't  this is a super cheap old-school side  scroller which looks like crazy fun to  play so count me in  okay i get why most of you are here you  want a free game well here it is e  football and to clarify i mean football  and not the version where you pick up  the ball and run with it e football has  been through some changes and as of  september it will be free to play  completely on all platforms if it looks  familiar it's because the name  e-football has changed many times some  of you will know this as pez others as  pro-evo some will know this as winning  eleven it's had an identity crisis for  years now while konami has put  everything under one roof e-football is  what we're all calling it from now on  and they hope to follow in the steps of  battle royale games introducing a  free-to-play option with extras to  purchase it's still unclear if that  means there will be pay-to-win mechanics  or mystery loot boxes like in fifa so i  guess we wait and see a campaign mode is  in the works but the key to success is  flawless online play the exact date of  release is being revealed very soon in  fact it may be the same day i'm saying  this and if it is revealed i'll be sure  to update that in the info below  speaking of free games a quick note that  call of duty vanguard open beta is here  for us all on september the 18th running  over that weekend it's the perfect  opportunity to see if you want to play  more call of duty this year or you're  gonna switch to battlefield lucky i'm  battlefield okay if you're on  playstation then there is a gift for you  with this every ps4 and ps5 player will  have access to the alpha version running  from august 27th to 29th so if it's  already september this has passed but if  it's still august when you're watching  this and you're on playstation more free  stuff okay back to full price games  [Music]  did you ever play the award-winning life  is strange well six years later they are  still making those games this time its  life is strange true colours we watch  the journey of alex chen who is  desperately trying to hide her psychic  abilities which includes the power to  absorb emotions from others that she  meets  this game deals with death and coping  mechanisms so be prepared to cry your  eyes out after playing it don't worry if  you haven't played the previous games  this is a new story knowing the last six  years of content is not vital although  it would help life is strange true  colours hits you in the fields on  september the 10th on every single  platform you can imagine except the  samsung smart fridge rip  [Music]  diablo 2 resurrected comes back from the  dead this year a remaster of a hugely  successful action role-playing game made  21 years ago taking charge of a  selection of heroes and fighting through  three zones of hordes before descending  into hell to fight diablo himself of  course there's more to it than that the  rpg elements and item management is the  core hook and an interesting gothic  horror story accompanies you throughout  for a nostalgia hit of the good old days  diablo 2 resurrected is perfect but  selling this game to new players will be  the biggest obstacle they face  if you want to tunnel down to hell for a  firefight with fear look out for diablo  2 resurrected on september 23rd on  playstation xbox pc and even the switch  has a version okay a few notable  mentions the annual basketball of thon  nba 2k slams down this month on  september the 10th wrc 10 drives in your  face on september the 2nd and if you're  waiting for the new rainbow six game  this month it's been delayed to january  2022 oh  [Music]  well oh here's a game series i think is  worth your time lost judgment the yakuza  game series have been around longer than  most of us yet even with a huge fan base  most people still don't know about it in  2018 a spin-off to the series sprang up  which told the story through the eyes of  a detective investigating murder cases  and other things youtube won't let me  say it's far more hard hitting than the  yakuza franchise but it still retains  the sense of wonderment searching  through japanese locations and the  free-flowing combat is so addicting and  now we have the sequel lost judgement  continuing the yakuza side story  allowing us to stalk more shady  underworld figures lost judgment arrives  on the 24th of september on ps4 and ps5  and the xbox series  [Music]  finally they've done it again one month  after the director's cut of ghost of  tsushima we have another director's cut  this time death stranding death  stranding was the game that lets you  urinate on liquid tar monsters and walk  across the usa with bionic legs in every  way you can imagine it it was weird and  i loved it set after most of the world  had died out death stranding asks us to  reconnect america and find a way to  fight back against the bt creatures  plaguing the world and now the  director's cut is here to take the base  game up to ps5 with a bunch of new  updates including a bodybot you no  longer need to do this all alone look at  him so there we have it eight new games  coming in september 21. any catch you  fancy i'm going to try e football fist  and i really hope keena bridge of  spirits releases this month if you're  still here please write the name of the  first console you ever owned in your  entire life i will try and find you and  give you some feedback i'm adam you're  awesome i'll see you next time  [Music]

